abstract: >
  z-pinch-postproc is a pure-Python toolkit for Z-pinch fusion reactor
  design with two integrated modules: a yield post-processor that
  computes engineering metrics (fusion yield, target gain, engineering
  gain, Lawson triple product, burn duration, stagnation pressure) from
  1D radiation-MHD profile data; and a blanket neutronics calculator
  (TBR — tritium breeding ratio) using both a fast parametric formula
  (~milliseconds) calibrated against real OpenMC Monte Carlo transport
  (~1-2 minutes per design point). The v1.5.0 release includes
  hybrid fission blanket support (U-238 layer), Z-FFR (Peng 2014)
  spherical geometry validation, and three documented honest negative
  findings (Fe reflector hurts in cylindrical, U-238 HURTS TBR, no
  smooth closed-form for mult_inside=False geometry).
